  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Periodic adult preventive visit completed</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed and the prevention plan updated. Her cervical cytology two years ago was normal, so the next screen is due in a year. She has no record of HIV or hepatitis C testing. Sun protection and hearing protection in the cockpit discussed. [S]<list><item>HIV and hepatitis C tests today.</item><item>Broad-spectrum sunscreen and sunglasses for long flights.</item><item>Influenza vaccine in the autumn.</item><item>Next preventive visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Chronic rhinosinusitis without nasal polyps (J32.9)</content>. The acute exacerbation has settled with the culture-sensitive antibiotic, but the chronic blockage and loss of smell persist after four weeks of irrigation and the nasal steroid; SNOT-22 44. The planned end-of-course phone check was missed; she was improving, so no harm resulted. She should stay on the medical plan until the CT at about ten weeks. [S]<list><item>Continue saline irrigation twice daily and fluticasone daily.</item><item>Sinus CT and review in about six weeks.</item><item>Fly only when she is free of blockage and pressure; no sedating antihistamines.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Blood pressure screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>110/70 mmHg</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-2 score 0</td></tr><tr><td>Anxiety screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No anxiety symptoms on interview</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy alcohol use screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>AUDIT-C score 0</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco use</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Never smoked</td></tr><tr><td>Cervical cancer screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Cytology two years ago normal; every three years at ages 21 to 29, next due in a year</td></tr><tr><td>Contraception and pregnancy intention</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Copper intrauterine device in place for two years; not planning a pregnancy</td></tr><tr><td>Folic acid</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Counseled that 0.4 mg daily is advised for anyone who could become pregnant; she will start it if she plans a pregnancy</td></tr><tr><td>Intimate partner violence screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Negative; she feels safe</td></tr><tr><td>Chlamydia and gonorrhea screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Age 25 with no partner at present and no new partner since her last negative test</td></tr><tr><td>HIV and hepatitis C screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>No result on record; once-in-a-lifetime tests drawn today with her agreement</td></tr><tr><td>Diabetes and cholesterol screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Age 25 with a BMI of 19.0 and no risk factors</td></tr><tr><td>Sun protection and hearing protection</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Sunscreen and sunglasses for long flights; noise-reducing headset in use</td></tr><tr><td>Influenza vaccine</td><td>Due</td><td>To be given in the autumn, when the new season&apos;s vaccine arrives</td></tr><tr><td>COVID-19 vaccine</td><td>Due</td><td>Discussed; she will decide in the autumn, with the influenza vaccine</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus, diphtheria, and pertussis</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Tdap six years ago</td></tr><tr><td>Measles, mumps, rubella, varicella, and hepatitis B</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Childhood series documented</td></tr><tr><td>HPV vaccine</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Series completed in adolescence</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Guideline basis: Clinical practice guideline (update): adult sinusitis (2015); International consensus statement on allergy and rhinology: rhinosinusitis 2021 (2021); Guide for Aviation Medical Examiners: Over-the-Counter (OTC) Medications Reference Guide, What OTC Medications Can I Take and Still Be Safe to Fly? (2024); Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026); USPSTF A and B Recommendations (2026); Adult Immunization Schedule by Medical Condition and Other Indication (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: HIV and hepatitis C results by phone. Sinus CT and review in about six weeks. Next preventive visit in one year. Next scheduled visit 2026-08-17: review after ten weeks of medical therapy: symptom score, sinus CT result, and the decision about surgery. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
